  M4 CANDIDATE [C-friendship maya_singh turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "You want my honest read? We're stronger than we look. People forget that about themselves."
    NPC: "Come see what I found. You won't believe it."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: You walk to the hollow with Maya. Nothing much there — but they talk the whole way, and you learn the shape of them a little better.
    YOU: "I’ll come back to help."
    NPC: "Wait — I'm away from Haven right now, out on the road. I can't promise a dawn meet from out here — find me when I'm back and we'll set it then."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Just catching up, really. Nothing to sum up."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: They let the words sit there, unanswered.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: They let that thread drop — for now.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "So what's your plan here? Just... get through it?"
    YOU: "One day at a time."
    NPC: "Honest. I can work with honest."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Mine's simple: learn one useful thing a week. This week it's making do. A plan's just a direction you argue with."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Small talk, that's all. Nothing worth repeating."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Okay — I need to move. But I'm glad we talked."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: They glance at the fire, then back. The quiet doesn't seem to bother them.
    NPC: "...Think about it? I'll be around."
    NPC: "Take care out there."

