  M4 CANDIDATE [C-friendship gen_oppmpym turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Any regrets? The real kind, not the small stuff."
    YOU: "I didn't say what I needed to say. To someone. Now I can't."
    NPC: Quiet. "Yeah. I think everyone's carrying one of those."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: The ease drains out of it, a little.
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "I regret the ordinary days I rushed through. All those Columbus, Ohio mornings I spent annoyed at small things. I'd pay anything for one annoyed morning now."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on your regrets."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "What got you through the first week? The very first days."
    YOU: "Honestly? Shock. Just kept moving."
    NPC: "Shock's underrated. It's the body's way of buying you time."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "Spite, mostly. Pure, clean spite at the sky. Then someone shared food with me and the spite turned into something else. I still don't have a word for the something else."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — we're still on your regrets."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on your regrets. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "I've got things to see to. Don't be a stranger."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: "You're a good listener, you know that?" A tired smile.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Take care out there."

