  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request wanjiru_kamau turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Wood Sorrel — I keep thinking about what you said. I'm seeing it everywhere now."
    NPC: "Can I ask you something? ... I want us to stick together. Properly. Watch each other's backs."
    YOU: "Yes. Stick together."
    NPC: "Stick together, then." They look steadier already.
    YOU: (listen)
    NPC: "Well." A breath. "That's where things stand."
    YOU: (listen)
    NPC: "So." They look at the fire for a moment.
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on that plant lesson."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: Something in them stays shut, for now.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "When's the last time you really laughed?"
    YOU: "Recently — someone tripped over nothing and we all lost it. It felt like stealing."
    NPC: "Stealing joy. I like that. We should steal more of it."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Three days ago. Someone dropped a whole basket of tubers and we just stood there laughing. It wasn't even funny. It was the standing there."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on that plant lesson."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

