  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request olivia_bennett turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Can we talk?" Olivia sits down near you. "Just... talk. Like people used to."
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: A flicker at the corner of their mouth. Not quite a smile. Not quite anything.
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "Ha." Not amused. "So you figured it out. Yeah, I took 2× Stick. What are you going to do about it?"
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Any regrets? The real kind, not the small stuff."
    YOU: "I didn't say what I needed to say. To someone. Now I can't."
    NPC: Quiet. "Yeah. I think everyone's carrying one of those."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: Something eases in their shoulders. They're really talking to you now.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "I regret the ordinary days I rushed through. All those Melbourne, Australia mornings I spent annoyed at small things. I'd pay anything for one annoyed morning now."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on your regrets. Worth considering."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — we're still on your regrets."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on your regrets. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Want to come with us?"
    NPC: "Okay. Yeah. I trust you."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "I wish we had longer. Soon, yeah?"
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "This was good." They mean it.

